            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Tamil for a son or daughter, then the Tamil for to adopt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: கொஞ்சு",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கொஞ்சு — koñcu — \"to coo over; to fondle\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "தாத்தா பேத்தியைக் கொஞ்சினார். tāttā pēttiyaik koñciṉār. Grandfather cooed over his granddaughter."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): கொஞ்சினேன், koñciṉēṉ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also of a child’s sweet prattle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கொஞ்சு (koñcu) is native Dravidian (DEDR 2043), for loving baby talk and fondling."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
